From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:01:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 140/148] hjviewer: the type scale's roles in place of raw
 sizes (UX-S3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U52: HjvText (common/hjv_style.dart) gains caption (13/400/1.45),
captionStrong (13/600/1.35) and dialogTitle (18/700/1.4). The raw sizes of
the app's own lines take the role of the same size and weight: HjvCallout's
title and text, the alert frame's and the update alert's title, the toast,
dialog.dart's hjvDialogTextStyle, hjvFieldLabel, the fields' help and error
and the 2FA secret, msgboxContent's text, the access dialogs (_checking, the
support code's lines), the account window, the peer cards' titles and lines,
the update screen and its About rows, the remote readiness card, the incoming
connections list and, after U15, the file rows' date (caption) and size
(bodySmall) in hjv_session_look.dart. A line height within 0.05 of the role's
becomes the role's; 1.5 (the dialogs' text) and the 12 px paragraphs' 1.45
stay. Sizes with no role keep their number (the ID and code displays, the
phone card's 15, the CM window's fitted 12 px lines). The lines with a raw
fontSize in hjv_*/hjviewer_* files go from 56 to 28.

U47 stage 2: hjvKeepAll on the widget side for the update screen's body,
hints and notes (page and alert), the update dialogs (B1, the move to Play,
[지금 업데이트]), the peer update card's lines, the account window's
remaining paragraphs and lines (this PC's line, the password line, the
devices' and uses' lines, the new device notice, the login notice, the
wake dialog, the login-ended dialog) and the desktop left pane's install
card, whose text is an upstream ko.rs tip. Never inside _t, never in a
SelectableText or SelectionArea.

Tests: hjviewer_style_test.dart checks the three roles,
hjviewer_session_look_test.dart the file row's date and size. The two
bridge-needing widget tests read the kept texts through hjvKeepAll; this also
fixes their five failures on the base (texts that earlier lanes put through
hjvKeepAll or HjvCallout, and HjvCallout's close_rounded icon).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
